  "content": {
    "title": "Vanderbilt women's basketball blows out High Point in first round of March Madness",
    "text": "Updated March 21, 2026, 7:53 p.m. CTVanderbilt basketball advanced to the second round of Women's March Madness with a 102-61 blowout win over No. 15 seed High Point on March 21 at Memorial Gymnasium.The No. 2 seed Commodores (28-4) got off to a fast start and never looked back. National leading scorer Mikayla Blakes scored 30 points, giving her the Vanderbilt single-season scoring record. It was her 13th 30-point performance this season and gave her the Vanderbilt single-season scoring record.Sacha Washington (10 points, 17 rebounds, four assists) and Ndjakalenga Mwenentanda (10 points, 11 rebounds) put up double-doubles. Freshman Aubrey Galvan had 17 points and six assists in her first taste of March Madness.High Point (27-6) saw guard Macy Spencer score 27.Vanderbilt will face either No. 7 seed Illinois or No. 10 seed Colorado in the second round on March 23, with a chance to advance to the Sweet Sixteen in Fort Worth. Watch Vanderbilt vs High Point live with Fubo (free trial)Vanderbilt vs High Point score updates Vanderbilt vs High Point score update: Mikayla Blakes gets 30 pointsMikayla Blakes re-entered the game for the fourth quarter and got up to 30 points with a pair of free throws. She then subbed out of the game with Vanderbilt's lead over 30 points. Vanderbilt vs High Point score update: Commodores cruisingVanderbilt led, 81-47, at the end of the third quarter. Mikayla Blakes came out of the game after scoring 28 in favor of several bench players. Vanderbilt vs High Point score update: Lead balloons over 30Vanderbilt built up its lead to 69-37 at the third quarter media timeout with 4:44 to go in the third quarter. Mikayla Blakes is up to 28 points and Macy Spencer up to 25. Vanderbilt vs High Point score update: Commodores build leadVanderbilt held a 50-27 lead during the second-quarter media timeout, leading 50-27 with 2:49 to go in the quarter. Mikayla Blakes is up to 21 points, setting a Commodores single-season record for points scored, and Macy Spencer has 22. Vanderbilt vs High Point score update: Commodores lead comfortably after first quarterVanderbilt held a 30-13 lead after the end of the first quarter, with Mikayla Blakes up to 13 points with two assists. Macy Spencer leads High Point with 11. Vanderbilt vs High Point score update: Panthers get a few threesHigh Point went on a 6-0 run and cut Vanderbilt's lead to 20-11 with two 3-pointers from Macy Spencer, who has nine of the Panthers' 11 points at the media timeout with 4:20 to go in the first quarter. Vanderbilt vs High Point score update: Commodores get off to a hot startVanderbilt went on an 11-0 run, leading 16-2 after a Mikayla Blakes 3-pointer was changed to a two and prompting High Point to take a timeout with 6:38 left in the first quarter. Mikayla Blakes already has seven points. Vanderbilt vs High Point starting lineupsVanderbiltG Mikayla BlakesG Aubrey GalvanG Justine PissottG Ndjakalenga MwenentandaF Sacha WashingtonHigh PointG Brecken SnotherlyG Macy SpencerG Anna HagerG Aaliyah CollinsF Nevaeh Zavala What time does Vanderbilt vs High Point play today? Date: Saturday, March 21Time: 6 p.m. CTLocation: Memorial GymnasiumWhat channel is Vanderbilt vs High Point game on today? TV channel: ESPNewsStreaming: Fubo (subscribe today)Radio: 94.9 The Fan and the Vanderbilt Athletics appVanderbilt vs High Point prediction Vanderbilt 95, High Point 59 Vanderbilt vs High Point injury updates Vanderbilt will have its full roster available save Madison Greene, who is out for the season.For High Point, Lexi Fleming, Olivia Medford and Sanai Cole are out.Vanderbilt basketball first, second round schedule in NCAA tournamentSaturday, March 21Game 1: No. 15 High Point vs. No. 2 Vanderbilt, 6 p.m. CTGame 2: No. 10 Colorado vs. No. 7 Illinois, 8:15 p.m. CTMonday, March 23Game 1 winner vs. Game 2 winner, TBD Where is High Point University?High Point University is in High Point, North Carolina, part of the Piedmont Triad region.Aria Gerson covers Vanderbilt athletics for The Tennessean. Contact her at agerson@gannett.com or on X, formerly Twitter, @aria_gerson.We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.",
